IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `sta-strata`
IMPORT `sta-qa`

-- Strata Titles Act 1985 (WA) -- cases for the Q&A layer (sta-qa.l4): every exported question, for every role and
-- every situation. Generated by the scratchpad script qa/b13/gen_sta_cases.py; the expected values were written by hand
-- from the deposited text and are in that script.
--
-- Each question is asked for each role it is not about, with every other input an ASSUMEd value that has none: the
-- answer must be `does not arise for you`, and reading any of those inputs would stop the evaluation with an error ("it
-- is an assumed term"). Each question with a situation input is asked, for its own role, with the situation FALSE and
-- every later input ASSUMEd, and must answer `does not arise for you`. Where the situation holds, each question is asked
-- on facts worked by hand, and once against the baseline export's own answer on the same facts.
--
-- One limit (graffiti finding 31): the baseline reads `Kind of resolution` and `My dispute` through OTHERWISE, so for
-- those an ASSUMEd value that is read would not be caught. Every situation input is a BOOLEAN, read before anything else.
--
-- Facts are the baseline's: Chloe (c094), Daniel (d037) and Jake (k076), with the encoder's figures for unit
-- entitlements, budgets and lot counts. The seller's and the occupier's facts are HYPOTHETICAL.
--
-- BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Cases -- the Q&A layer`

ASSUME `an unasked fact` IS A BOOLEAN
ASSUME `an unasked number` IS A NUMBER
ASSUME `an unasked fund` IS A `Fund`
ASSUME `an unasked resolution` IS A `Kind of resolution`
ASSUME `an unasked kind of by-law` IS A `Kind of by-law`
ASSUME `an unasked by-law` IS A `What the by-law does`
ASSUME `an unasked change` IS A `What changed before settlement`
ASSUME `an unasked variation` IS A `Notifiable variation`
ASSUME `an unasked dispute` IS A `My dispute`

`as the owner` MEANS `I own a lot in a strata titles scheme`
`as the buyer` MEANS `I am buying a lot in a strata titles scheme, or have just bought one`
`as the seller` MEANS `I am selling a lot in a strata titles scheme`
`as the occupier` MEANS `I rent or occupy a lot in a strata titles scheme, and do not own it`


`a quiet-hours by-law` MEANS `What the by-law does` WITH
    `is beyond any power to make it` IS FALSE
    `is inconsistent with the Act or another written law` IS FALSE
    `is inconsistent with a restricted use condition` IS FALSE
    `denies or limits a member's vote` IS FALSE
    `restricts selling, leasing, mortgaging or passing on a lot` IS FALSE
    `discharges or modifies an easement or restrictive covenant` IS FALSE
    `restricts an assistance animal of a person with a disability` IS FALSE
    `is unfairly prejudicial, discriminatory, oppressive or unreasonable, as the Tribunal finds` IS FALSE

`a ban on dogs that covers assistance dogs` MEANS `What the by-law does` WITH
    `is beyond any power to make it` IS FALSE
    `is inconsistent with the Act or another written law` IS FALSE
    `is inconsistent with a restricted use condition` IS FALSE
    `denies or limits a member's vote` IS FALSE
    `restricts selling, leasing, mortgaging or passing on a lot` IS FALSE
    `discharges or modifies an easement or restrictive covenant` IS FALSE
    `restricts an assistance animal of a person with a disability` IS TRUE
    `is unfairly prejudicial, discriminatory, oppressive or unreasonable, as the Tribunal finds` IS FALSE

`a ban on leasing lots` MEANS `What the by-law does` WITH
    `is beyond any power to make it` IS FALSE
    `is inconsistent with the Act or another written law` IS FALSE
    `is inconsistent with a restricted use condition` IS FALSE
    `denies or limits a member's vote` IS FALSE
    `restricts selling, leasing, mortgaging or passing on a lot` IS TRUE
    `discharges or modifies an easement or restrictive covenant` IS FALSE
    `restricts an assistance animal of a person with a disability` IS FALSE
    `is unfairly prejudicial, discriminatory, oppressive or unreasonable, as the Tribunal finds` IS FALSE

`Jake's unit entitlement grows on registration` MEANS `What changed before settlement` WITH
    `the notified area of the lot` IS 50
    `the area of the lot now` IS 50
    `the notified unit entitlement` IS 30
    `the notified sum of unit entitlements` IS 2000
    `the unit entitlement now` IS 32
    `the sum of unit entitlements now` IS 2000
    `termination proposal papers were served on the seller` IS FALSE
    `the scheme plan was modified affecting the lot or common property` IS FALSE
    `the by-laws were modified` IS FALSE
    `a services contract was entered or varied` IS FALSE
    `a lease or licence over common property was granted or varied` IS FALSE

`a unit entitlement change under 5%` MEANS `What changed before settlement` WITH
    `the notified area of the lot` IS 50
    `the area of the lot now` IS 50
    `the notified unit entitlement` IS 30
    `the notified sum of unit entitlements` IS 2000
    `the unit entitlement now` IS 31
    `the sum of unit entitlements now` IS 2000
    `termination proposal papers were served on the seller` IS FALSE
    `the scheme plan was modified affecting the lot or common property` IS FALSE
    `the by-laws were modified` IS FALSE
    `a services contract was entered or varied` IS FALSE
    `a lease or licence over common property was granted or varied` IS FALSE

-- Impossible zero sums of unit entitlements (s 37(1)), which the form's engine tries: the layer answers without
-- dividing (after the independent check, 6 Nov 2026).
GIVEN `notified sum` IS A NUMBER
      `sum now` IS A NUMBER
      `area now` IS A NUMBER
      `termination papers` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `What changed before settlement`
`a change with sums of unit entitlements` `notified sum` `sum now` `area now` `termination papers` MEANS `What changed before settlement` WITH
    `the notified area of the lot` IS 50
    `the area of the lot now` IS `area now`
    `the notified unit entitlement` IS 0
    `the notified sum of unit entitlements` IS `notified sum`
    `the unit entitlement now` IS 0
    `the sum of unit entitlements now` IS `sum now`
    `termination proposal papers were served on the seller` IS `termination papers`
    `the scheme plan was modified affecting the lot or common property` IS FALSE
    `the by-laws were modified` IS FALSE
    `a services contract was entered or varied` IS FALSE
    `a lease or licence over common property was granted or varied` IS FALSE

`nothing changed` MEANS `What changed before settlement` WITH
    `the notified area of the lot` IS 50
    `the area of the lot now` IS 50
    `the notified unit entitlement` IS 30
    `the notified sum of unit entitlements` IS 2000
    `the unit entitlement now` IS 30
    `the sum of unit entitlements now` IS 2000
    `termination proposal papers were served on the seller` IS FALSE
    `the scheme plan was modified affecting the lot or common property` IS FALSE
    `the by-laws were modified` IS FALSE
    `a services contract was entered or varied` IS FALSE
    `a lease or licence over common property was granted or varied` IS FALSE



